    :graph/usage-guide {:guide/purpose "Detect worsening ETA past-due ratios per country (latest vs previous completed PST snapshot), attribute the increase to vendors, explain it by ETA code / ETA source, and find owners, high-risk PO lines and notification recipients."
      :guide/asset-scope "Read-only ClickHouse aggregates over past_due.vendor_past_due_daily, past_due.past_due_detail_view, past_due.vendor_master_mapping_view and past_due.vendor_eta_notification_contact; current and historical (date-range) views."
      :guide/applicability "Countries are analysed independently (US, CA in scope). Snapshots strictly before the current PST date only. Relative change is (latest - previous) / previous; a zero previous ratio yields null plus zero-baseline-increase."
      :guide/limitations ["Legacy v2 entries retain calendar-day behavior; v3 uses explicit calendar mode." "v3 SQL selects Vendor Top N and computes ETA Top-5/Other summaries before paging." "Read and reconcile every facts/check page; returned-result completeness alone is insufficient." "Permissions/RLS must be enforced by the actual deployment; Skill allowlists are not access control." "No cross-query transaction or production usability claim without live validation."]
      :guide/composition "Standalone Graph with one logical SQL Source Slot (eta-clickhouse); no dependencies."
